   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = x^{2} \\) and \\( dv = \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), so \\( du = 2 x \\, dx \\) and \\( v = - \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            [
               "Cos",
               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then the integral equals \\( \\left[- x^{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\pi} - \\int_{0}^{\\pi} - 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\), and the boundary term is \\( \\pi^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Power",
            "Pi",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The remaining integral \\( \\int_{0}^{\\pi} - 2 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} \\, dx \\) needs integration by parts once more, with the polynomial factor as the new u; it equals \\( 4 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So the value is \\( \\pi^{2} - \\left(4\\right) = -4 + \\pi^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
